<title>USA: Thermo Cardiosystems Q1 shr $0.05 vs $0.08.</title>
<headline>Thermo Cardiosystems Q1 shr $0.05 vs $0.08.</headline>
<dateline>WOBURN, Mass. 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended</p>
<p>					  Mar 29, 1997   Mar 30, 1996(a)</p>
<p> Revenues			     $14,902,000	 $15,405,000</p>
<p>Income Before Provision for</p>
<p>  Income Taxes			  3,073,000	   5,222,000</p>
<p> Net Income			     1,875,000	   3,431,000</p>
<p> Earnings per Share			   .05		   .08</p>
<p> Weighted Average Shares	   40,256,000	  40,905,000</p>
<p>(a) Historical results have been restated to reflect the acquisition of International Technidyne Corp from Thermo Electron Corp, accounted for in a manner similar to a pooling of interests.</p>
<p>Thermo Cardiosystems is a publicly-held subsidiary of Thermedics Inc, a company in the Thermo Electron group.</p>
<p>--((New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
